<title>LEBANON: Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 468.7 bln pounds.</title>
<headline>Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 468.7 bln pounds.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's weekly treasury bill issue of December 5 raised 468.7 billion Lebanese pounds, the finance ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>The previous issue raised 568.4 billion pounds.</p>
<p>The new issue posted a nominal surplus of subscription against maturity of 221 billion pounds. It raised the following amounts (in billions of pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term			  Yield		    Amount</p>
<p>    Three months	    14.36 (14.39)	   86.9  (48.7)</p>
<p>    Six months		16.48 (16.55)	   58.9  (94.6)</p>
<p>    12 months		 17.50 (17.57)	   57.5  (91.9)</p>
<p>    24 months		 20.76 (21.00)	  265.4 (333.2)</p>
<p>The Lebanese pound closed at 1,553.5 to the U.S. dollar on Monday from 1,554 a week earlier and 1,599 a year ago.</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602057 645456</p>
